    "script": "A client wants real-time notifications shipped by Friday. Here's the entire build, no cuts.\nStep one: the schema. One notifications table, a boolean for read state, a foreign key back to users.\nStep two: scaffold the socket server. One command wires socket dot io straight into the existing auth middleware.\nBefore writing any logic, the agent writes the failing test first: user A sends, user B receives it in under two hundred milliseconds.\nRed first. Then the broadcast handler goes in, and that same test turns green on the very next run.\nStep three: the client. An eight line hook that reconnects automatically the moment the socket drops.\nShip it to iOS and Android from the exact same codebase. Zero separate mobile build.\nBefore merge, the full suite runs: forty-one tests, zero flaky, six seconds total.\nOne last check. Pull it up in Chrome, click send, watch the badge update live.\nFinal tally: eleven files changed, one migration, zero new dependencies added.\nThat's a real feature, shipped in one sitting, not a demo reel.\nFollow for the next build, start to finish."
